%% Every query uses one incidence grammar: an open, query-indexed span whose
%% covered native coordinates are supplied by the registered anchors.  The
%% span adapts to a cell, row, grid, terminal readout, trace, carrier, or layer,
%% but never changes into a completeness brace, causal arrow, or proof path.
%% A not-evaluated query replaces the ordinary index gap with the same broken
%% stop used in the query endpoint.  The exact dependency remains immediately
%% above it in the query-local `blocked by' field, where long phonological
%% names can wrap without invading the first-order grid.
